WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.520
The second day is over.

00:07.520 --> 00:23.260
You have now eight more left to work, to work diligently, ardently.

00:23.260 --> 00:32.340
Second day, slightly better than the first day, slightly better.

00:32.340 --> 00:38.800
The difficulties are still there.

00:38.800 --> 00:46.140
What a wandering mind, a fleeting mind, a flickering mind.

00:46.140 --> 01:11.380
So instable, so unstable, so infirm, so agitated, no peace, no tranquility, so wild, like a wild animal, a monkey mind,

01:11.380 --> 01:29.100
grasping one branch after the other, one branch after the other, one object after the other, one object after the other, highly agitated, certainly very wild,

01:29.100 --> 01:34.380
like a wild bull, a wild elephant.

01:34.380 --> 01:58.460
When it comes in the midst of a human society, dwellings of human beings, it proves so dangerous, it creates havoc, so harmful.

01:58.540 --> 02:10.820
But an experienced person, a wise person, trains this wild elephant, the wild bull,

02:10.820 --> 02:23.620
trains this wild elephant, the wild bull, working very patiently, patiently and persistently.

02:23.700 --> 02:37.860
And once this wild animal is tamed, trained, all its enormous strength comes to serve the human society.

02:37.860 --> 02:42.260
It starts serving the human society.

02:42.340 --> 02:54.740
Its strength was a great danger to the human society, and now this very strength turns into a great service to the human society.

02:54.740 --> 03:12.180
Similarly, this wild mind, so long as it remains untrained, untamed, very dangerous, very dangerous, very harmful.

03:12.180 --> 03:26.180
And if you somehow train it, tame it, its enormous strength starts helping us.

03:26.180 --> 03:44.180
And the strength of the mind, in comparison with the strength of a wild elephant, many more times it is stronger, more powerful.

03:44.180 --> 03:51.300
And no one can harm us more than our own wild mind.

03:51.300 --> 04:02.100
And no one can help us more than our own trained mind, tamed mind, disciplined mind.

04:02.100 --> 04:16.100
But as it requires a lot of patience to train a wild elephant, one who is experienced in training the wild elephant or wild bull,

04:16.100 --> 04:26.100
does not get irritated, does not develop anger or hatred towards this wild animal, very patiently.

04:26.100 --> 04:34.100
Very patiently. One works very patiently, but persistently.

04:34.100 --> 04:44.100
Similarly, you have to deal with your wild mind very patiently.

04:44.100 --> 04:52.100
You want to get it trained in one day, or two days, or no, no.

04:52.100 --> 05:00.100
And you become irritated because it is not getting trained. Look, I have given two days of my life and yet it is not getting trained.

05:00.100 --> 05:08.100
You become irritated, irritated, it becomes more wild, it becomes more dangerous.

05:08.100 --> 05:12.100
Patience. You have to work very patiently.

05:12.100 --> 05:24.100
But persistently, persistently, continuously, continuously, ultimately you will win.

05:24.100 --> 05:32.100
The mind is bound to get disciplined. But you have to work.

05:32.100 --> 05:40.100
No one else can work for you. You have to fight out your own battle.

05:40.100 --> 05:46.100
You have to work out your own salvation, your own liberation.

05:46.100 --> 05:52.100
None else can do that for you.

05:52.100 --> 06:06.100
Someone who has been successful in controlling the mind, someone who has become successful in purifying the mind,

06:06.100 --> 06:18.100
someone who has become liberated, enlightened, with all the compassion and love, this person will show the path.

06:18.100 --> 06:22.100
But you have to walk on the path.

06:22.100 --> 06:32.100
You have to take every step on the path yourself. Step by step, step by step, you have to reach the final goal.

06:32.100 --> 06:36.100
Nobody will take you on his shoulder to the final goal.

06:36.100 --> 06:43.100
Nobody can take anyone else on the shoulder and reach the final goal. Impossible.

06:43.100 --> 06:47.100
Each individual has to work.

06:47.100 --> 06:59.100
Of course, when you start taking steps on the path of Dhamma, the path of liberation, the path of enlightenment,

06:59.100 --> 07:02.100
the law of nature is such.

07:02.100 --> 07:11.100
The universal law of nature is such that you get tuned up with the good vibrations of saintly people,

07:11.100 --> 07:17.100
good vibrations of Dhamma, and you get all the inspiration and the strength.

07:17.100 --> 07:23.100
You start getting so much support. I know it with my own personal experience.

07:24.100 --> 07:31.100
And also the experience of so many students, you will get support.

07:31.100 --> 07:37.100
You call it grace, you call it mercy, you call whatever you like. You will get support.

07:37.100 --> 07:47.100
But still, every step you have to take on the path. You have to take every step on the path.

07:48.100 --> 07:55.100
An incident in the life of Gautama Adi Buddha.

07:55.100 --> 08:07.100
At that time he was dwelling in a big meditation center in the city of Sravasti, capital of the state of Kosala.

08:07.100 --> 08:13.100
Large number of monks and nuns will come and learn Viparshana from him.

08:13.100 --> 08:21.100
Large number of householders, men, women will come and learn this technique from him, get benefited.

08:23.100 --> 08:30.100
Someone who used to come only in these evening discourses, but never practiced,

08:30.100 --> 08:39.100
he came one day little earlier when Buddha was alone, came to him, paid respect, and said,

08:40.100 --> 08:46.100
One question keeps on bothering me, and I hesitate to ask you, and there are so many people around.

08:46.100 --> 08:51.100
Now that you are alone, permit me to ask the question.

08:51.100 --> 08:58.100
Oh, go ahead. There should not be any confusion in your mind so far as Dhamma is concerned. Go ahead.

08:58.100 --> 09:04.100
And he said, Sir, I am coming here for a number of years.

09:05.100 --> 09:10.100
I understand what you teach. It is good.

09:10.100 --> 09:16.100
But I examine the people who come here to learn.

09:16.100 --> 09:25.100
I have noticed that some of them have really become fully liberated, fully enlightened.

09:25.100 --> 09:35.100
It is quite clear with their behavior, with their lifestyle, with their dealings with these people, situations.

09:35.100 --> 09:38.100
It is very clear they are liberated people.

09:38.100 --> 09:47.100
And quite a few are not fully liberated, and yet a big change has come in their life.

09:47.100 --> 09:52.100
I notice it. A big change for the better has come.

09:53.100 --> 10:01.100
But then, Sir, there are people like me, no change.

10:01.100 --> 10:04.100
We are as we were.

10:04.100 --> 10:14.100
My question is, Sir, you are so powerful, you are so compassionate.

10:14.100 --> 10:19.100
Somebody coming to you, taking refuge in you,

10:19.100 --> 10:24.100
why don't you use all your power and your compassion to liberate us?

10:24.100 --> 10:27.100
Why somebody remains unliberated or half-liberated?

10:27.100 --> 10:31.100
Please, Sir, this question bothers me.

10:31.100 --> 10:33.100
Buddha smiled.

10:33.100 --> 10:39.100
This is what he kept on teaching, but people do not want to understand what can he do.

10:39.100 --> 10:42.100
So he explained.

10:42.100 --> 10:49.100
And his way of explanation was always different according to the caliber of the mind of the student who has come.

10:49.100 --> 10:53.100
At times he will answer by counter-questioning.

10:53.100 --> 10:57.100
So in this case also he started counter-questioning.

10:57.100 --> 10:59.100
Hey, from where are you?

10:59.100 --> 11:03.100
Sir, I am from Sravasti, this city, the capital of Koshala.

11:03.100 --> 11:05.100
Oh, no, no.

11:05.100 --> 11:10.100
Your facial features say that you are not from this country.

11:10.100 --> 11:14.100
You are from some other state and you have come and settled down here.

11:14.100 --> 11:16.100
Oh, yes, Sir, you are quite correct.

11:16.100 --> 11:20.100
Actually I belong to Magadha, Rajgiri.

11:20.100 --> 11:24.100
I have come and settled down here last few years.

11:24.100 --> 11:25.100
Good.

11:25.100 --> 11:34.100
Having come and settled down here, have you severed all relations with Rajgiri, with Magadha?

11:34.100 --> 11:36.100
You don't go there anymore?

11:36.100 --> 11:38.100
Oh, no, Sir, I keep going there.

11:38.100 --> 11:42.100
I still have my relatives there, I have my friends there, I have my business there.

11:42.100 --> 11:44.100
I keep going there.

11:44.100 --> 11:47.100
Every year I go many times to Rajgiri and come back.

11:47.100 --> 11:52.100
I say, you keep going from here to Rajgiri.

11:52.100 --> 11:59.100
So certainly you must be knowing very well the path from here to Rajgiri because you have walked over the path so many times.

11:59.100 --> 12:03.100
Yes, Sir, I know the path so well.

12:03.100 --> 12:11.100
Now tell me, having settled down in this part of the country, you must have made many friends.

12:11.100 --> 12:15.100
And out of these many friends some have become very intimate to you, isn't it?

12:15.100 --> 12:18.100
Yes, Sir, some have become very intimate.

12:18.100 --> 12:24.100
Those who are very intimate, they certainly should be knowing that you don't belong to this part.

12:24.100 --> 12:30.100
You are actually from Magadha, from Rajgiri, and you have come and settled down here.

12:30.100 --> 12:36.100
And they also must be knowing that you keep going to Rajgiri and coming back every year so many times.

12:36.100 --> 12:38.100
Yes, Sir.

12:38.100 --> 12:41.100
Then these people know that you know the path from here to Rajgiri very well.

12:41.100 --> 12:43.100
Yes, Sir.

12:43.100 --> 12:49.100
Some of them must be asking you, how about this path? What kind of path?

12:49.100 --> 12:53.100
Do you keep it a top secret or do you explain what top secrets are?

12:53.100 --> 12:55.100
I explain them very clearly.

12:55.100 --> 13:04.100
You start from here, from Sravasti, start moving eastwards, and you move this way, that way, you turn this way, that way, and you will reach Varanasi.

13:04.100 --> 13:09.100
And then you keep moving this way, that way, turn here, there, you will reach Kaya.

13:09.100 --> 13:12.100
And then you keep moving this, and you will reach Rajgiri.

13:12.100 --> 13:15.100
I explain the whole path very clearly.

13:15.100 --> 13:17.100
Very clearly?

13:17.100 --> 13:21.100
That means everyone to whom you have explained the path must have reached Rajgiri.

13:21.100 --> 13:24.100
How is that possible, Sir?

13:24.100 --> 13:28.100
If someone has not walked on the path, how will he reach Rajgiri?

13:28.100 --> 13:32.100
Young man, this is what I keep on telling every day.

13:32.100 --> 13:38.100
People come to me, understanding very well that this is a person who is fully liberated.

13:38.100 --> 13:40.100
He has reached the final goal.

13:40.100 --> 13:42.100
He knows the path from here to the final goal.

13:42.100 --> 13:44.100
They come to me.

13:44.100 --> 13:47.100
They ask me, what is the path?

13:47.100 --> 13:49.100
Why I keep it as a top secret?

13:49.100 --> 13:52.100
I explain them very clearly.

13:52.100 --> 13:56.100
This is how you walk, this is how you walk, and you will get this station and this station,

13:56.100 --> 14:01.100
and you keep walking, keep walking, and you will reach the final goal.

14:01.100 --> 14:10.100
Someone just listens and says, Sadhu, Sadhu, Sadhu, and bows down three times,

14:10.100 --> 14:13.100
but won't take a single step on the path.

14:13.100 --> 14:15.100
How will this person reach the goal?

14:15.100 --> 14:16.100
What can I do?

14:16.100 --> 14:19.100
I have shown the path, my job is done.

14:19.100 --> 14:22.100
Somebody has started taking steps on the path.

14:22.100 --> 14:25.100
Someone has taken just one step on the path.

14:25.100 --> 14:29.100
This person is one step nearer the goal.

14:29.100 --> 14:31.100
Someone has taken 100 steps on the path.

14:31.100 --> 14:35.100
This person is 100 steps nearer the goal.

14:35.100 --> 14:39.100
Someone has taken all these steps on the path, has reached the goal.

14:39.100 --> 14:45.100
Each individual has to take steps on the path.

14:45.100 --> 14:50.100
No one else can do that, no one else.

14:50.100 --> 14:58.100
If I am thirsty and someone else drinks water, my thirst will not get quenched.

14:58.100 --> 15:01.100
For quenching my thirst, I must drink water.

15:01.100 --> 15:08.100
If I am sick and someone else takes medicine, my sickness will not get cured.

15:08.100 --> 15:11.100
How to take medicine myself? So simple.

15:11.100 --> 15:16.100
And yet, we don't want to work.

15:16.100 --> 15:22.100
And we just expect some other supernatural power to be very kind, to do something for us.

15:22.100 --> 15:26.100
It doesn't work, doesn't work.

15:26.100 --> 15:30.100
Each individual has to work out one's own salvation.

15:30.100 --> 15:35.100
Each individual has to take every step on the path.

15:35.100 --> 15:47.100
And he explains, in his own words, the Pali, the language that he spoke, the language of India of those days.

16:05.100 --> 16:15.100
You have to work diligently, ardently for your liberation.

16:15.100 --> 16:22.100
Someone who has become Tathagat, that means one has become liberated.

16:22.100 --> 16:29.100
The literal meaning Tathagat, one has reached the final goal of ultimate truth, the eternal truth.

16:29.100 --> 16:31.100
One has reached that goal.

16:31.100 --> 16:37.100
He will very compassionately point out to the path, this is the path.

16:37.100 --> 16:40.100
Akha Taro, he will just point out, this is the path.

16:40.100 --> 16:44.100
Akha Taro Tathagat.

16:44.100 --> 16:52.100
Everyone who has reached that goal will only point out the path.

16:52.100 --> 16:55.100
But each individual has to walk on the path.

16:55.100 --> 17:00.100
Each individual has to work out one's own salvation.

17:00.100 --> 17:07.100
If this is accepted, and earlier one accepts it, the better.

17:07.100 --> 17:13.100
One accepts that I have to walk on the path, every step I have to take to reach the final goal.

17:13.100 --> 17:16.100
Then the question comes, what is the path?

17:16.100 --> 17:19.100
And how to walk over it?

17:19.100 --> 17:21.100
And he explains.

17:21.100 --> 17:23.100
He kept on explaining.

17:23.100 --> 17:25.100
This is what he did the whole life.

17:25.100 --> 17:31.100
He kept on explaining the path, the Dhamma.

17:31.100 --> 17:34.100
Dhamma means law.

17:34.100 --> 17:36.100
Dhamma means truth.

17:36.100 --> 17:40.100
Dhamma means nature.

17:40.100 --> 17:45.100
The law of nature, universal law of nature,

17:45.100 --> 17:51.100
which governs the entire universe, animate, inanimate,

17:51.100 --> 17:56.100
is never sectarian, universal.

17:56.100 --> 18:02.100
One has to understand what is this law, what is this nature.

18:02.100 --> 18:07.100
One has to understand that if I break the law, I get punished.

18:07.100 --> 18:11.100
Then I'm there.

18:11.100 --> 18:18.100
If I live a life in line with the law, in accordance to the law, I start getting rewarded.

18:18.100 --> 18:22.100
I start moving towards the final goal of liberation.

18:22.100 --> 18:26.100
And this is the path.

18:26.100 --> 18:36.100
Someone came to him and asked him, sir, in few words, few simple words, tell me what is the path.

18:36.100 --> 18:39.100
I can't understand high philosophies and all that.

18:39.100 --> 18:44.100
And Buddha smiled. Dhamma is not for high philosophies.

18:44.100 --> 18:48.100
It is for people to practice.

18:48.100 --> 18:50.100
So they must understand what it is.

18:50.100 --> 18:56.100
If they don't understand and simply play intellectual game with it, it doesn't help.

18:56.100 --> 18:59.100
Dhamma is always explained in very simple words.

18:59.100 --> 19:01.100
All right, I will again explain you.

19:01.100 --> 19:12.100
And he explained in few words, again in his own words, in the language that he spoke in those days.

19:12.100 --> 19:28.100
Sabhapapa Sayakaranam Kusala Sayupasampada

19:28.100 --> 19:35.100
Sachetparyudapana

19:35.100 --> 19:42.100
Etang Buddhanasasana

19:42.100 --> 19:47.100
Etang Buddhanasasana

19:47.100 --> 19:49.100
Sasana is the teaching.

19:49.100 --> 19:52.100
Buddhana, all the Buddhas.

19:52.100 --> 19:56.100
This is the teaching of all the Buddhas.

19:56.100 --> 20:00.100
Have you ever said this is my teaching?

20:00.100 --> 20:03.100
Buddha is not a name of somebody.

20:03.100 --> 20:07.100
Buddha means an enlightened person, a liberated person.

20:07.100 --> 20:10.100
His name was Gautama.

20:10.100 --> 20:16.100
And to become Buddha is not more or less you have only one person.

20:16.100 --> 20:19.100
Not just only Gautama can become Buddha.

20:19.100 --> 20:21.100
Anyone can become Buddha.

20:21.100 --> 20:24.100
Of course it is not that easy.

20:24.100 --> 20:26.100
Can this person become Buddha?

20:26.100 --> 20:28.100
No.

20:28.100 --> 20:30.100
Very hard work.

20:30.100 --> 20:32.100
Very hard work.

20:32.100 --> 20:36.100
Yet, doing hard work, hard work, hard work,

20:36.100 --> 20:42.100
there is every possibility of everyone becoming a fully enlightened person becoming Buddha.

20:42.100 --> 20:48.100
And when someone becomes a Buddha, he will teach this and nothing else.

20:48.100 --> 20:53.100
This will be the teaching of every enlightened person.

20:53.100 --> 20:55.100
What is it?

20:55.100 --> 21:00.100
Sab papas ay karanam

21:00.100 --> 21:03.100
Ay karanam, abstain.

21:03.100 --> 21:09.100
Sab, all, papas, all sinful activities.

21:09.100 --> 21:16.100
Abstain from all sinful activities, unwholesome activities.

21:16.100 --> 21:23.100
And kusalas se upasampadha

21:23.100 --> 21:29.100
Perform wholesome actions, pious actions.

21:29.100 --> 21:33.100
Enter the field of piety, upasampadha.

21:33.100 --> 21:38.100
Get ordained in piety, upasampadha.

21:38.100 --> 21:42.100
And say chitthe pariyodapanam

21:42.100 --> 21:44.100
Keep on purifying your mind.

21:44.100 --> 21:46.100
Keep on purifying your mind.

21:46.100 --> 21:48.100
That's all.

21:48.100 --> 21:52.100
Abstain from unwholesome sinful actions.

21:52.100 --> 21:56.100
Perform wholesome pious actions.

21:56.100 --> 22:00.100
And keep on purifying your mind.

22:00.100 --> 22:05.100
The entire dhamma and totality is contained in it.

22:05.100 --> 22:08.100
Nothing is missing.

22:08.100 --> 22:11.100
You won't have to add anything to this.

22:11.100 --> 22:15.100
That is why it is called paripunam, complete.

22:15.100 --> 22:18.100
It is complete.

22:18.100 --> 22:21.100
And you won't have to take out anything from it.

22:21.100 --> 22:25.100
There is not even a dot which is wrong, which has to be taken out.

22:25.100 --> 22:28.100
That is why it is called parishuddham.

22:28.100 --> 22:31.100
So pure, ultra pure.

22:31.100 --> 22:33.100
Nothing to take out from it.

22:33.100 --> 22:35.100
Nothing to add to it.

22:35.100 --> 22:37.100
This is dhamma.

22:37.100 --> 22:40.100
Abstain from sinful actions.

22:40.100 --> 22:42.100
Perform pious actions.

22:42.100 --> 22:44.100
Purify the mind.

22:44.100 --> 22:49.100
Every religion worth the name will say the same thing.

22:49.100 --> 22:52.100
But then...

22:52.100 --> 22:58.100
When an enlightened person teaches dhamma, he teaches universal dhamma.

22:58.100 --> 23:00.100
He will never teach sectarian.

23:00.100 --> 23:02.100
Universal dhamma.

23:02.100 --> 23:04.100
Eternal dhamma.

23:04.100 --> 23:06.100
The law of nature is eternal.

23:06.100 --> 23:11.100
It was there so in the past, it is so present, it will be so in the future.

23:11.100 --> 23:14.100
And it is applicable to one and all.

23:14.100 --> 23:17.100
That is dhamma.

23:17.100 --> 23:24.100
But out of madness, out of ignorance, people forget the essence of dhamma.

23:24.100 --> 23:27.100
And they make a sect out of it.

23:27.100 --> 23:31.100
Then this sect, or this sect, or this sect.

23:31.100 --> 23:35.100
Then these very words will start carrying different meanings.

23:35.100 --> 23:37.100
Everyone will recite the same thing.

23:37.100 --> 23:40.100
Abstain from sinful actions.

23:40.100 --> 23:44.100
No religion will say you keep on performing sinful actions.

23:44.100 --> 23:47.100
Everyone will say the same thing.

23:47.100 --> 23:49.100
Perform wholesome action, pious action.

23:49.100 --> 23:52.100
Every religion, every tradition will say that.

23:52.100 --> 23:54.100
Purify your mind.

23:54.100 --> 23:57.100
Every religion, every tradition, everyone will say that.

23:57.100 --> 24:01.100
But yet, a big difference.

24:01.100 --> 24:07.100
A big difference in the explanations.

24:07.100 --> 24:10.100
What is sin?

24:10.100 --> 24:14.100
And what is piety?

24:14.100 --> 24:21.100
When dhamma turns into a sect, then that particular sect,

24:21.100 --> 24:25.100
the so-called religious people of that particular sect,

24:25.100 --> 24:29.100
the so-called pious people of this particular sect,

24:29.100 --> 24:34.100
they may be wearing this kind of robe or that kind of robe.

24:34.100 --> 24:37.100
May be having this rosary or that rosary.

24:37.100 --> 24:41.100
May be having this mark over the forehead or that mark over the forehead.

24:41.100 --> 24:45.100
This external appearance or that external appearance.

24:45.100 --> 24:48.100
Now people belonging to this particular sect will say,

24:48.100 --> 24:53.100
those who have this kind of external appearance are pious people.

24:53.100 --> 24:55.100
Others are not.

24:55.100 --> 25:00.100
Definition is given, a wrong definition is given.

25:00.100 --> 25:02.100
Another definition.

25:02.100 --> 25:08.100
Every sect, people belonging to that particular sect,

25:08.100 --> 25:12.100
will perform this kind of rite or that kind of ritual,

25:12.100 --> 25:15.100
this religious ceremony or that religious ceremony.

25:15.100 --> 25:19.100
Every sect will have different rites, different rituals, different ceremonies.

25:19.100 --> 25:22.100
And those belonging to a particular sect will say,

25:22.100 --> 25:27.100
those who are performing these rites, these rituals, these ceremonies,

25:27.100 --> 25:30.100
oh, they are pious people.

25:30.100 --> 25:35.100
And those who do not, they are not pious, they are sinful.

25:35.100 --> 25:44.100
Another mad definition is given for sin and piety.

25:44.100 --> 25:50.100
One more definition is given, which is still more confusing.

25:50.100 --> 25:58.100
Every sect has some belief, some dogma, some philosophy.

25:58.100 --> 26:02.100
We believe in this philosophy, this dogma.

26:02.100 --> 26:06.100
Those who believe in this dogma and this philosophy are very pious people.

26:06.100 --> 26:10.100
Those who do not believe, they are not pious people.

26:10.100 --> 26:18.100
Such kind of definitions of sin and piety harm dhamma.

26:18.100 --> 26:20.100
Dhamma is no more dhamma.

26:20.100 --> 26:26.100
In dhamma, the definition is universal, not sectarian.

26:26.100 --> 26:31.100
External appearances will differ from sect to sect, from person to person.

26:31.100 --> 26:36.100
Rites, rituals, ceremonies will differ from person to person, from sect to sect.

26:36.100 --> 26:42.100
A philosophical belief may differ from person to person, from sect to sect.

26:42.100 --> 26:45.100
But the definition of dhamma cannot differ.

26:45.100 --> 26:51.100
It is universal, and it is eternal.

26:51.100 --> 26:57.100
What is sin? What is unwholesome action?

26:57.100 --> 27:06.100
Any action, physical or vocal, any action that you perform,

27:06.100 --> 27:12.100
and it harms and hurts other beings,

27:12.100 --> 27:21.100
it disturbs the peace and harmony of other beings, is a sinful action, is an unwholesome action.

27:21.100 --> 27:26.100
And what is a pious action? What is a wholesome action?

27:26.100 --> 27:33.100
Every action, physical or vocal, which supports, helps other beings

27:33.100 --> 27:40.100
in living a peaceful, harmonious atmosphere, which does not disturb their peace, their harmony,

27:40.100 --> 27:49.100
which does not harm them, does not hurt them, is a pious action, wholesome action.

27:49.100 --> 27:55.100
This definition is universal.

27:55.100 --> 28:05.100
As one keeps going deeper in dhamma, at the experiential level, it becomes so clear

28:05.100 --> 28:14.100
that this is in line with the law of nature, in line with the law of nature.

28:14.100 --> 28:24.100
The first abstain from all sinful action is called sila, living the life of morality.

28:24.100 --> 28:32.100
Don't perform any action, physical or vocal, which will harm other beings.

28:32.100 --> 28:37.100
Live a moral life.

28:37.100 --> 28:42.100
Perform wholesome actions.

28:42.100 --> 28:52.100
And the most wholesome action is to be master of your mind, never remain slave of your mind.

28:52.100 --> 28:59.100
Learn how to concentrate your mind, one-pointedness,

28:59.100 --> 29:08.100
at the base of wholesomeness, without having anything against anybody, anger or hatred or ill-will.

29:08.100 --> 29:15.100
This is the most wholesome action.

29:15.100 --> 29:21.100
This becomes very clear as one starts taking steps on the path.

29:21.100 --> 29:26.100
Look, the teaching is so universal, so universal.

29:26.100 --> 29:33.100
The first is called sila, the second is called samadhi, and the third purification of the mind is called panya,

29:33.100 --> 29:40.100
that means wisdom, insight, direct experience of the truth inside,

29:40.100 --> 29:49.100
and developing the wisdom of the law, the universal law, and changing the habit pattern of the mind at the deepest level.

29:49.100 --> 29:53.100
Now the first sila, morality.

29:53.100 --> 29:57.100
Initially one starts understanding it merely at the intellectual level.

29:57.100 --> 30:06.100
Yes, I should not perform any action at the physical level or vocal level, which will harm other beings.

30:06.100 --> 30:13.100
For example, if someone comes and hits me, kills me, I certainly don't like it.

30:13.100 --> 30:19.100
I don't like it. So if I hit others or kill others, this person will not like.

30:19.100 --> 30:24.100
So I should not do anything which I don't want others to do for me.

30:24.100 --> 30:32.100
I should not kill. This will hurt others, harm others.

30:32.100 --> 30:39.100
If someone steals away, robs away certain thing which belongs to me and which is very dear to me, I don't like it.

30:39.100 --> 30:46.100
I feel hurt. Therefore, I should not steal anything belonging to somebody else.

30:47.100 --> 30:53.100
This will hurt this person. I should not do it.

30:53.100 --> 31:06.100
Someone rapes or has sexual misconduct with a member of my family, I don't like it. I get hurt.

31:06.100 --> 31:11.100
Similarly, I should not do the same thing. Others will get hurt.

31:11.100 --> 31:17.100
If someone speaks lies and tries to deceive me, I don't like it.

31:17.100 --> 31:20.100
I should not speak lie and try to deceive others.

31:20.100 --> 31:24.100
If someone speaks harsh words, I don't like it.

31:24.100 --> 31:28.100
I should not speak harsh words to others. They won't like it.

31:28.100 --> 31:41.100
And then, although I understand and everyone understands that one should not do this, should not do that,

31:41.100 --> 31:54.100
but when one gets intoxicated by any drug or by liquor, one is helpless, one is a slave of that particular intoxication

31:54.100 --> 31:59.100
and will perform all those actions which one does not want to perform.

31:59.100 --> 32:04.100
And yet one performs, I should not take any kind of intoxicants.

32:04.100 --> 32:11.100
This is what one understands at the surface level of the mind, at the intellectual level of the mind.

32:11.100 --> 32:18.100
Again one starts understanding, again at a little deeper level, but again at the intellectual level.

32:19.100 --> 32:28.100
A human being is a social being. He has to live in the society, live with the members of the family and others.

32:30.100 --> 32:43.100
If he keeps on performing such actions which disturb the entire atmosphere around, creates disharmony everywhere, disturbs the peace everywhere,

32:43.100 --> 32:47.100
how can this person enjoy peace and harmony?

32:49.100 --> 33:00.100
If I ignite fire all around, all around there is fire, burning fire, how can I expect the cool, the tranquility within myself?

33:00.100 --> 33:08.100
Not possible. So I must help the atmosphere to be more peaceful, more tranquil,

33:08.100 --> 33:13.100
and then only I can experience peace and tranquility living in that atmosphere.

33:14.100 --> 33:17.100
Yes, it becomes clearer.

33:18.100 --> 33:25.100
But the dhamma becomes really clear when one starts practicing it.

33:26.100 --> 33:32.100
And an enlightened person takes one to that depth where one starts experiencing the law of nature.

33:33.100 --> 33:45.100
It will become so clear at the experiential level that whenever I perform any action, physical or vocal, which has harmed other people,

33:45.100 --> 33:52.100
I cannot perform that unless I have generated tremendous amount of negativity in my mind.

33:53.100 --> 33:58.100
I can't kill somebody unless I generate anger, hatred, ill-will, animosity.

33:58.100 --> 34:02.100
I cannot steal anything unless I have generated a lot of greed.

34:03.100 --> 34:07.100
I cannot commit sexual misconduct unless I have generated patience.

34:08.100 --> 34:15.100
And like this, maybe ego, maybe jealousy, some impurity or the other I must develop in my mind,

34:15.100 --> 34:24.100
and then only I perform a vocal or physical action which will harm others by experience.

34:25.100 --> 34:30.100
One who is walking on the path of dhamma will start understanding it by experience

34:31.100 --> 34:37.100
and will also start understanding that whenever I generate any negativity in the mind,

34:38.100 --> 34:45.100
anger, hatred, ill-will, animosity, passion, fear, ego, jealousy, greed, any impurity in my mind,

34:46.100 --> 34:50.100
nature does not want it. It goes against the law of nature.

34:50.100 --> 34:55.100
And nature starts punishing me. I get the punishment here and now.

34:56.100 --> 35:02.100
After death, a punishment will come. Leave that aside. We don't say that, don't believe it, but leave it aside.

35:03.100 --> 35:12.100
You will get punishment here and now. Every individual who started walking on the path will start realizing nature started punishing me.

35:13.100 --> 35:18.100
Because when I generate anger, I become so agitated, so unhappy, so miserable.

35:18.100 --> 35:24.100
It is impossible that I generate anger and feel very peaceful, feel full of tranquility.

35:24.100 --> 35:30.100
Impossible. I am bound to become agitated. Similarly, any defilement, I am bound to become agitated.

35:30.100 --> 35:34.100
Law of nature is such. Nature has started punishing me.

35:35.100 --> 35:42.100
And if I refrain from, abstain from these kinds of activities and don't generate these defilements in the mind,

35:43.100 --> 35:48.100
nature starts rewarding me. I feel so peaceful. It becomes so clear.

35:48.100 --> 35:55.100
This is the law of nature. Don't harm others. Don't hurt others.

35:55.100 --> 36:00.100
Don't perform any action at the physical or vocal level which will disturb others.

36:01.100 --> 36:05.100
Because you do not know, you have started harming yourself.

36:06.100 --> 36:09.100
You are the first victim of your action.

36:09.100 --> 36:12.100
You want to kill somebody. You generate anger.

36:12.100 --> 36:16.100
When you generate anger, you are being punished then and there.

36:16.100 --> 36:20.100
You are the first victim of your own anger, your own defilement.

36:20.100 --> 36:25.100
This becomes clearer and clearer to somebody who walks on the path of Dhamma.

36:26.100 --> 36:32.100
Then at a deeper level, because when I started experiencing the truth inside,

36:33.100 --> 36:39.100
the behavior pattern, the way of life starts changing automatically.

36:40.100 --> 36:44.100
Because one is not experiencing the truth inside,

36:45.100 --> 36:49.100
all the time one gives importance to things outside, outside, outside.

36:49.100 --> 36:52.100
One does not know how nature has started punishing me.

36:52.100 --> 36:55.100
One does not know how nature has started rewarding me.

36:55.100 --> 36:57.100
One does not know at all.

36:58.100 --> 37:02.100
Now with this practice, which we will learn for these ten days,

37:02.100 --> 37:05.100
it will become clearer and clearer.

37:05.100 --> 37:08.100
And once it becomes clearer at the experiential level,

37:08.100 --> 37:11.100
not merely at the intellectual level,

37:11.100 --> 37:14.100
not merely at the devotional level because Buddha said so,

37:14.100 --> 37:18.100
or our founder of our religion said so, or scripture says so,

37:18.100 --> 37:23.100
that doesn't work at the experiential level, the direct experience.

37:23.100 --> 37:27.100
Then it is something like you put your hand on the fire and your hand burns.

37:27.100 --> 37:32.100
Now you know, putting the hand on the fire, touching the fire, hurts me.

37:32.100 --> 37:35.100
Next time you are very careful not to put your hand on the fire.

37:35.100 --> 37:38.100
You don't like your hand to get burned.

37:38.100 --> 37:41.100
So you will keep away from this.

37:41.100 --> 37:44.100
You will start experiencing it deep within yourself

37:44.100 --> 37:50.100
that whenever you hurt others, before hurting anybody, you started hurting yourself.

37:50.100 --> 37:53.100
You started burning inside.

37:53.100 --> 37:57.100
The hellfire within you starts burning you here and now.

37:57.100 --> 38:04.100
And when you live, a wholesome action, a good action, which helps others.

38:04.100 --> 38:09.100
The kingdom of heaven within, you start enjoying the peace,

38:09.100 --> 38:13.100
the peace, the tranquility of the kingdom of heaven within.

38:13.100 --> 38:17.100
The hell is within. The heaven is within.

38:17.100 --> 38:20.100
And this one starts experiencing.

38:20.100 --> 38:26.100
And this helps one to practice Dhamma properly,

38:26.100 --> 38:32.100
abstain from all evil actions, perform wholesome actions.

38:35.100 --> 38:42.100
The path is explained in detail, how you will walk on the path step by step.

38:43.100 --> 38:48.100
The whole path is called, in the language of those days,

38:48.100 --> 38:54.100
Aryo Athangiko Maggo. Maggo means path.

38:54.100 --> 38:58.100
Aryo, noble, noble path.

38:58.100 --> 39:06.100
Noble path in the sense that anyone who walks on the path is bound to become a noble person.

39:06.100 --> 39:10.100
He may belong to this country or that country, this community or that community.

39:10.100 --> 39:15.100
This color or that color, this gender or that gender, makes no difference.

39:15.100 --> 39:21.100
Anyone who walks on the path is bound to become a noble person, a saintly person,

39:21.100 --> 39:25.100
a good-hearted person, a pure-hearted person.

39:25.100 --> 39:31.100
That is why it is called noble path. Eightfold, eightfold noble path.

39:31.100 --> 39:34.100
Now this is divided in three divisions.

39:35.100 --> 39:38.100
Sheela, samadhi, panya.

39:38.100 --> 39:41.100
Sheela, morality.

39:41.100 --> 39:49.100
Don't perform any action at the physical or vocal level which will harm others.

39:49.100 --> 39:53.100
Three parts of the path come in this morality.

39:53.100 --> 39:55.100
Sheela.

39:55.100 --> 39:58.100
Samma, vacha.

39:58.100 --> 40:01.100
Samma, kammanta.

40:01.100 --> 40:04.100
Samma, ajiva.

40:04.100 --> 40:07.100
The word samma means right. Right.

40:07.100 --> 40:09.100
Samma, vacha.

40:09.100 --> 40:15.100
The speech, the speech must be right, wholesome.

40:15.100 --> 40:18.100
How can you know what is wholesome, what is unwholesome?

40:18.100 --> 40:23.100
If you know what is unwholesome and you abstain from it, what remains is wholesome.

40:23.100 --> 40:31.100
What is unwholesome, so far as speech is concerned, your vocal action is concerned,

40:31.100 --> 40:34.100
you abstain from speaking lies.

40:34.100 --> 40:38.100
This is unwholesome if you speak lies.

40:38.100 --> 40:42.100
You abstain from speaking harsh words which hurt others.

40:42.100 --> 40:45.100
It does not help them in any way.

40:45.100 --> 40:49.100
Because if you do that, it is unwholesome.

40:49.100 --> 40:53.100
You abstain from speaking words or backbiting.

40:53.100 --> 40:59.100
Two persons are friends and you hear something from here and then say something else to the other person

40:59.100 --> 41:04.100
and then you hear something, you break their friendship, make them enemies,

41:04.100 --> 41:08.100
you have performed unwholesome action.

41:08.100 --> 41:12.100
Or you just talk slanderous words, unwholesome action.

41:12.100 --> 41:17.100
Useless words, wasting your time, wasting the time of others, unwholesome vocal action.

41:17.100 --> 41:22.100
You abstain from all these and what remains is the wholesome action.

41:22.100 --> 41:26.100
Sama vaja, wholesome vocal action.

41:26.100 --> 41:32.100
Sama kammanta, wholesome physical action.

41:32.100 --> 41:34.100
Same yardstick.

41:34.100 --> 41:40.100
Any action which hurts and harms other beings is unwholesome.

41:40.100 --> 41:45.100
You abstain from that and what remains is wholesome.

41:45.100 --> 41:47.100
Don't kill.

41:47.100 --> 41:50.100
Don't steal.

41:50.100 --> 41:53.100
Don't perform sexual misconduct.

41:53.100 --> 41:57.100
Don't take any kind of intoxicants.

41:57.100 --> 42:02.100
If you abstain from that, then all your physical actions are wholesome, automatically wholesome.

42:02.100 --> 42:06.100
What remains is wholesome.

42:06.100 --> 42:11.100
Sama ajiva, right livelihood.

42:12.100 --> 42:16.100
Unless one is a monk or a nun or a recluse or a hermit,

42:16.100 --> 42:22.100
in that case one goes out with a begging bowl and doesn't keep anything with him or her.

42:22.100 --> 42:26.100
But a householder is not supposed to go out with a begging bowl.

42:26.100 --> 42:30.100
Has to work to earn livelihood.

42:30.100 --> 42:37.100
And work hard and work honestly without harming others.

42:37.100 --> 42:41.100
Now the same yardstick, without harming others.

42:41.100 --> 42:53.100
Your profession, your dealings must be such that yes, you get your remuneration from that,

42:53.100 --> 42:56.100
but it does not harm others.

42:56.100 --> 43:02.100
If you get a lot of profits in your business and that business is harming others,

43:02.100 --> 43:07.100
it is not sama ajiva, not sama ajiva.

43:07.100 --> 43:11.100
If your means of livelihood is such,

43:11.100 --> 43:16.100
which encourages other people to break shila and live an immoral life,

43:16.100 --> 43:19.100
and disturb the peace and harmony of others,

43:19.100 --> 43:23.100
it is not a sama ajiva, not a right livelihood.

43:23.100 --> 43:36.100
For example, someone starts doing business of arms, ammunitions, guns, bullets, bombs, atom bombs, hydrogen bombs.

43:36.100 --> 43:39.100
One gets a lot of money, good profit.

43:39.100 --> 43:45.100
But anyone who buys will use it for killing others.

43:45.100 --> 43:49.100
Not a good livelihood, not a right livelihood.

43:49.100 --> 43:53.100
Someone says, I don't kill. Yes, you don't kill.

43:53.100 --> 43:55.100
But you help others to kill.

43:55.100 --> 43:57.100
You are encouraging others to kill.

43:57.100 --> 44:01.100
Not right livelihood.

44:01.100 --> 44:12.100
Someone deals in flesh or meat, fish, and says, I don't kill.

44:12.100 --> 44:14.100
Somebody else has killed.

44:14.100 --> 44:16.100
You are encouraging someone else to kill.

44:16.100 --> 44:18.100
Not right livelihood.

44:18.100 --> 44:25.100
One deals in animals, grazes animals, and then gives it to the butcher.

44:25.100 --> 44:27.100
He kills. I don't kill.

44:27.100 --> 44:29.100
No, you are encouraging it.

44:29.100 --> 44:32.100
Not right livelihood.

44:32.100 --> 44:34.100
One deals in poison.

44:34.100 --> 44:37.100
Anyone who takes, makes use of it to kill others.

44:37.100 --> 44:38.100
Not right livelihood.

44:38.100 --> 44:40.100
Like this, anything.

44:40.100 --> 44:43.100
The commodity in which you are dealing,

44:43.100 --> 44:52.100
if it encourages others to break their shield, then your livelihood is not livelihood.

44:52.100 --> 45:00.100
Even certain livelihoods, which look quite wholesome,

45:00.100 --> 45:04.100
but the motivation is wrong.

45:04.100 --> 45:09.100
If the motivation is wrong, it becomes unwholesome.

45:09.100 --> 45:14.100
One incident in my life, years back, when I was not in contact with pure dharma,

45:14.100 --> 45:17.100
I never knew how to observe things inside.

45:17.100 --> 45:21.100
And yet I used to feel myself a very dharmic person, a very religious person,

45:21.100 --> 45:25.100
performing this rite, that ritual, this, this, giving this donation, that donation.

45:25.100 --> 45:28.100
I never knew pure dharma.

45:28.100 --> 45:31.100
It so happened, a member of the family became very ill,

45:31.100 --> 45:36.100
and it so happened that the family doctor was out of the station.

45:36.100 --> 45:38.100
I had to call some other doctor.

45:38.100 --> 45:42.100
The doctor was a very famous doctor, a very busy doctor.

45:42.100 --> 45:48.100
Whether he will agree to give a visit at home or not, let me go personally and persuade him.

45:48.100 --> 45:51.100
I went to him.

45:51.100 --> 45:54.100
Usually there is a big crowd of patients.

45:54.100 --> 45:56.100
Now I find nobody, he was just alone.

45:56.100 --> 46:00.100
Of course, I was happy that if he is alone, he will come.

46:00.100 --> 46:04.100
But out of curiosity I asked him, how is the doctor?

46:04.100 --> 46:07.100
Every day there is a long queue of patients in your dispensary.

46:07.100 --> 46:09.100
Today nobody is there.

46:09.100 --> 46:16.100
With a very long and sad face he says, this part, this season, this part of the year,

46:16.100 --> 46:19.100
always there is some epidemic or the other.

46:19.100 --> 46:21.100
I don't know what happened this year.

46:21.100 --> 46:23.100
There is no epidemic.

46:23.100 --> 46:25.100
I felt so bad.

46:25.100 --> 46:28.100
What a noble profession, a doctor's profession, a physician's profession,

46:28.100 --> 46:33.100
to serve others, to come out of illness, and look his motivation.

46:33.100 --> 46:35.100
He wants more and more epidemic to start.

46:35.100 --> 46:37.100
Not that all doctors are like that.

46:37.100 --> 46:39.100
We shouldn't condemn every doctor.

46:39.100 --> 46:41.100
But that was the case.

46:41.100 --> 46:43.100
And I felt very bad.

46:43.100 --> 46:48.100
But at that time I never knew how to observe the reality inside.

46:48.100 --> 46:52.100
So long as one does not know how to observe the reality inside,

46:52.100 --> 46:54.100
one keeps on finding fault with others.

46:54.100 --> 46:58.100
Look, so and so is so bad, so and so is so bad, so and so is so bad.

46:58.100 --> 47:02.100
When I started this technique, observing the truth inside,

47:02.100 --> 47:06.100
I found out I am worse than the doctor.

47:06.100 --> 47:09.100
I come from a business community, a business family,

47:09.100 --> 47:14.100
and we know the business people mostly.

47:14.100 --> 47:19.100
The motivation, they have got their own vocabulary.

47:19.100 --> 47:23.100
Suppose there is war or famine.

47:23.100 --> 47:25.100
Consumer goods are scarce.

47:25.100 --> 47:27.100
Prices start shooting up.

47:27.100 --> 47:30.100
In our language, commercial language, we say,

47:30.100 --> 47:32.100
Market is improving, wonderful.

47:32.100 --> 47:34.100
Market is improving.

47:34.100 --> 47:36.100
We get more price, more profit.

47:36.100 --> 47:38.100
Whatever stock you have got, we will bring more profit.

47:38.100 --> 47:40.100
Market is improving.

47:40.100 --> 47:42.100
No more famine, no more war.

47:42.100 --> 47:44.100
A lot of consumer goods.

47:44.100 --> 47:46.100
Market has gone down.

47:46.100 --> 47:48.100
And with a very sad heart, we will say,

47:48.100 --> 47:50.100
Oh, market is crushed.

47:50.100 --> 47:52.100
So bad, it is so bad.

47:52.100 --> 47:54.100
What attitude?

47:54.100 --> 47:56.100
What kind of motivation?

47:56.100 --> 47:58.100
We don't care whether people suffer or not.

47:58.100 --> 48:00.100
We must get our money.

48:00.100 --> 48:06.100
Oh, this one will not understand unless one starts observing the truth inside.

48:06.100 --> 48:08.100
One remains so much involved.

48:08.100 --> 48:10.100
So much involved in the madness.

48:10.100 --> 48:13.100
There is nothing wrong in doing business.

48:13.100 --> 48:19.100
One has to earn money, reasonably, without harming others.

48:19.100 --> 48:24.100
Provided one keeps on understanding that I am playing the role,

48:24.100 --> 48:28.100
an important role to serve the community in this particular way.

48:28.100 --> 48:30.100
One may be in any profession.

48:30.100 --> 48:34.100
But if one keeps on thinking that by this profession I am serving the society,

48:34.100 --> 48:37.100
and in return I get my remuneration from the society,

48:37.100 --> 48:40.100
then serving the society becomes more important.

48:40.100 --> 48:42.100
Remuneration will certainly come.

48:42.100 --> 48:44.100
Nothing wrong.

48:44.100 --> 48:47.100
A businessman buys from the manufacturer and distributes to the consumer.

48:47.100 --> 48:49.100
Nothing wrong in that.

48:49.100 --> 48:51.100
Every consumer cannot run to the manufacturer to buy his requirements.

48:51.100 --> 48:53.100
They must be a middleman.

48:53.100 --> 48:57.100
This middleman, if he starts thinking that I am here to exploit and get money,

48:57.100 --> 49:02.100
then this rat race of money, money, money, will make this person mad.

49:02.100 --> 49:05.100
Far away from dhamma, far away from dhamma.

49:05.100 --> 49:10.100
Some ajiva wants you to have a good volition,

49:10.100 --> 49:14.100
good motivation to earn money without harming others.

49:14.100 --> 49:16.100
Serving people, a member of the society,

49:16.100 --> 49:23.100
the society parts his or her own role to serve the society in the capacity that one can.

49:23.100 --> 49:30.100
All these three, samma vacha, samma kammanta, samma ajiva,

49:30.100 --> 49:34.100
right speech, right physical actions, and right livelihood,

49:34.100 --> 49:41.100
they all come in the first part of dhamma, shila, morality.

49:41.100 --> 49:48.100
If the teacher of dhamma had only taught this,

49:48.100 --> 49:51.100
then he was not an enlightened person.

49:51.100 --> 49:55.100
An enlightened person will teach the totality of dhamma.

49:55.100 --> 49:58.100
This is only partial dhamma.

49:58.100 --> 50:00.100
Just to teach people and tell them,

50:00.100 --> 50:05.100
oh you people of the world, you should not do this, you should not do this, you should not do this.

50:05.100 --> 50:08.100
You should do this, you should do this, you should do this.

50:08.100 --> 50:12.100
People will hear from this ear and it will go out of the other ear.

50:12.100 --> 50:14.100
It won't have any effect.

50:14.100 --> 50:20.100
Because one knows very well that I should not do this, I should not do this.

50:20.100 --> 50:23.100
And yet one keeps on doing the same thing.

50:23.100 --> 50:26.100
A drunkard knows very well that it is not good for me.

50:26.100 --> 50:30.100
I must come out with an addiction. It is so bad.

50:30.100 --> 50:33.100
A gambler knows very well I should not do this.

50:33.100 --> 50:37.100
And yet when the time comes, he forgets everything.

50:37.100 --> 50:40.100
He drinks, he gambles. Why?

50:40.100 --> 50:43.100
Because he has no control over the mind.

50:43.100 --> 50:46.100
He has no mastery over the mind.

50:46.100 --> 50:48.100
He is a slave of his own mind.

50:48.100 --> 50:52.100
He is a slave of his own behavior pattern deep inside.

50:52.100 --> 50:55.100
Dhamma is not complete just to give sermons like this.

50:55.100 --> 50:57.100
Just to talk of Sheila doesn't help.

50:57.100 --> 51:00.100
So the next step is Samadhi.

51:00.100 --> 51:04.100
Mastery over the mind.

51:04.100 --> 51:08.100
You have to learn how to become master of your own mind.

51:08.100 --> 51:12.100
You have to learn how to concentrate your mind.

51:12.100 --> 51:16.100
And concentrate your mind with the wholesome base.

51:20.100 --> 51:25.100
The concentration of mind with the base of purity.

51:25.100 --> 51:28.100
This is Samadhi.

51:28.100 --> 51:32.100
Another three parts of Dhamma come under this division of Samadhi.

51:32.100 --> 51:36.100
Samma Vayamu.

51:36.100 --> 51:39.100
Samma Sati.

51:39.100 --> 51:42.100
Samma Samadhi. Samma Vayamu.

51:42.100 --> 51:47.100
Right type of efforts. Right type of exercises.

51:47.100 --> 51:50.100
You have to take some exercises.

51:50.100 --> 51:54.100
When your body is weak, when your body is sick, unhealthy.

51:54.100 --> 51:59.100
So weak that you can't take even few steps. You keep on dangling here, dangling there.

51:59.100 --> 52:03.100
Somebody will ask you, advise you, take this exercise, this exercise.

52:03.100 --> 52:07.100
Make your muscles strong, make your body strong.

52:07.100 --> 52:11.100
Similarly when the mind becomes weak.

52:11.100 --> 52:15.100
And all of you have noticed two days, working two days.

52:15.100 --> 52:18.100
What a sick mind you are carrying.

52:18.100 --> 52:20.100
What a weak mind you are carrying.

52:20.100 --> 52:22.100
Dangling here, dangling there.

52:22.100 --> 52:26.100
So infirm, so unstable.

52:26.100 --> 52:32.100
You have to do some exercises to make it stable, firm, strong, healthy, sound.

52:32.100 --> 52:37.100
Any exercise which makes your mind healthy is a good exercise.

52:37.100 --> 52:40.100
This is Samma Vayamu.

52:40.100 --> 52:42.100
There are four exercises.

52:42.100 --> 52:46.100
In Dhamma every exercise is examine yourself.

52:46.100 --> 52:49.100
First exercise examine yourself.

52:49.100 --> 52:52.100
Oh, even at the surface level of the mind,

52:52.100 --> 52:58.100
at present I have got this voice, that voice, this voice, this voice.

52:58.100 --> 53:00.100
Get rid of them.

53:00.100 --> 53:02.100
Get rid of the voices which are there.

53:02.100 --> 53:04.100
First good exercise.

53:04.100 --> 53:07.100
Second exercise, again examine your mind.

53:07.100 --> 53:12.100
My mind does not carry this particular voice or this particular voice.

53:12.100 --> 53:14.100
Close all the doors of your mind.

53:14.100 --> 53:17.100
Whatever impurity is not there, don't allow it to come.

53:17.100 --> 53:19.100
Second good exercise.

53:19.100 --> 53:22.100
Third good exercise, again examine your mind.

53:22.100 --> 53:27.100
My mind has this particular virtue, that particular virtue.

53:27.100 --> 53:29.100
Don't develop ego because of that.

53:29.100 --> 53:32.100
Don't develop proud because of that.

53:32.100 --> 53:33.100
This virtue is there.

53:33.100 --> 53:35.100
This is the reality.

53:35.100 --> 53:40.100
Now I must see that I preserve it, I maintain it, and I multiply it.

53:40.100 --> 53:42.100
Again examine your mind.

53:42.100 --> 53:47.100
When you find that you don't have this particular virtue or that particular virtue,

53:47.100 --> 53:49.100
open all the gates of your mind. Welcome.

53:49.100 --> 53:52.100
This virtue which is not here should come in.

53:52.100 --> 53:59.100
These are the four healthy exercises to make the mind healthy, strong.

53:59.100 --> 54:02.100
This is what you started doing indirectly.

54:02.100 --> 54:07.100
And the next, sammasati, awareness.

54:07.100 --> 54:09.100
Right type of awareness.

54:09.100 --> 54:12.100
What is right type of awareness?

54:12.100 --> 54:16.100
The awareness of the reality of this moment

54:16.100 --> 54:22.100
pertaining to your own physical and mental structure is the right type of awareness.

54:22.100 --> 54:25.100
Awareness cannot be of the past.

54:25.100 --> 54:27.100
The word sati has got two meanings.

54:27.100 --> 54:33.100
One meaning is a memory which has nothing to do with this part of dhamma.

54:33.100 --> 54:36.100
A memory is of the past.

54:36.100 --> 54:38.100
You keep on thinking of the past.

54:38.100 --> 54:42.100
This is not sammasati, this is not right awareness.

54:42.100 --> 54:44.100
Awareness cannot be of the future.

54:44.100 --> 54:48.100
You will be just thinking, you will be just imagining, you will be just dreaming.

54:48.100 --> 54:50.100
Doesn't it help?

54:50.100 --> 54:55.100
Awareness is real when you are with the awareness of the reality of this moment

54:55.100 --> 55:03.100
as it has manifested itself from moment to moment, from moment to moment.

55:03.100 --> 55:08.100
And this reality must be pertaining to your own being.

55:08.100 --> 55:12.100
This mind, this matter, the combination of the two.

55:12.100 --> 55:15.100
This is what you started doing.

55:15.100 --> 55:19.100
You started observing your breath coming in, going out.

55:19.100 --> 55:21.100
From moment to moment, as it is.

55:21.100 --> 55:23.100
If it is deep, it is deep.

55:23.100 --> 55:25.100
If it is shallow, it is shallow.

55:25.100 --> 55:29.100
If it passes through left nostril, left nostril, right nostril, right nostril.

55:29.100 --> 55:31.100
Both the nostrils, both the nostrils.

55:31.100 --> 55:34.100
Just the reality as it is, as it is.

55:34.100 --> 55:39.100
Of course, for a new student, you are permitted.

55:39.100 --> 55:42.100
When you can't feel the breath which has become very subtle,

55:42.100 --> 55:47.100
then you are permitted to take a few intentional breathings, conscious breathings,

55:47.100 --> 55:51.100
slightly hard breathings, but just a few.

55:51.100 --> 55:54.100
And you are again to come to the natural breath, normal breath,

55:54.100 --> 56:01.100
so that you may, your capability, you develop your faculty

56:01.100 --> 56:06.100
to feel the subtlest breath very clearly, the softest breath very clearly.

56:06.100 --> 56:09.100
And you are with the reality as it is.

56:09.100 --> 56:12.100
Not as you want it to be, but as it is.

56:12.100 --> 56:16.100
And that is called yatha bhuta, as it is.

56:16.100 --> 56:18.100
From moment to moment, as it is.

56:18.100 --> 56:20.100
You have been doing that.

56:20.100 --> 56:26.100
And another thing, the whole path takes you from very gross,

56:26.100 --> 56:30.100
gross, intensified, solidified, apparent reality,

56:30.100 --> 56:32.100
because that is what you experience initially,

56:32.100 --> 56:39.100
and then you move, move towards subtler, subtler, subtler, subtler reality.

56:39.100 --> 56:44.100
Explore the entire field of this material structure

56:44.100 --> 56:49.100
from the grossest reality to the subtlest reality.

56:49.100 --> 56:55.100
Explore the entire field of the mental structure, the mind and the mental contents

56:55.100 --> 57:01.100
from the grossest reality, surface level, and then subtler, subtler, subtlest reality.

57:01.100 --> 57:04.100
In the language of those days, he said,

57:04.100 --> 57:10.100
olariku, from olariku to sukhumaa, sukhumaa.

57:10.100 --> 57:14.100
Every step must be towards sukhumaa, sukhumaa, sukhumaa.

57:14.100 --> 57:17.100
Subtlety, subtlety, subtlety.

57:17.100 --> 57:20.100
You cross the entire field of subtlety of mind and matter,

57:20.100 --> 57:24.100
then you experience something which is beyond mind and matter.

57:24.100 --> 57:27.100
The entire field of mind and matter, you will notice,

57:27.100 --> 57:32.100
you will notice is a field where things arise, pass, arise, pass, arise, pass.

57:32.100 --> 57:35.100
Some change, some change is taking place.

57:35.100 --> 57:38.100
There is a constant flux, a constant flow going on.

57:38.100 --> 57:41.100
But when you cross this field, nothing arises, nothing passes.

57:41.100 --> 57:45.100
This is something, the eternal, ultimate truth.

57:45.100 --> 57:47.100
You can't imagine.

57:47.100 --> 57:50.100
On the path of dhamma, nothing should be imagined,

57:50.100 --> 57:53.100
and nothing should be accepted because a Buddha said so,

57:53.100 --> 57:55.100
or because your teacher says so.

57:55.100 --> 57:57.100
That's it.

57:57.100 --> 58:01.100
And that experience will make you a totally changed person.

58:01.100 --> 58:05.100
Experience of that ultimate truth, even for a few seconds,

58:05.100 --> 58:09.100
turns one into a saintly person, naturally.

58:09.100 --> 58:12.100
And the entire path, as you are moving from the gross reality

58:12.100 --> 58:16.100
towards the subtler, subtler, is a process of purification.

58:16.100 --> 58:19.100
And you will understand as you proceed further on the path.

58:19.100 --> 58:23.100
So one thing, clear, that you are moving from the gross reality

58:23.100 --> 58:25.100
towards the subtle reality.

58:25.100 --> 58:28.100
But understand you can't create subtle reality.

58:28.100 --> 58:31.100
You have to leave it to the dhamma, you have to leave it to the nature.

58:31.100 --> 58:33.100
And nature will keep on working.

58:33.100 --> 58:39.100
So for you, whatever manifests itself, you are just aware of it.

58:39.100 --> 58:43.100
Initially you have to take few hard breaths, and you are aware of it.

58:43.100 --> 58:46.100
Then naturally the breath becomes subtler and subtler,

58:46.100 --> 58:48.100
softer and softer, finer and finer.

58:48.100 --> 58:50.100
You are aware of it.

58:50.100 --> 58:55.100
Now, today, the whole day, you are aware of the touch of the breath

58:55.100 --> 58:57.100
within this limited area.

58:57.100 --> 58:59.100
You have chosen a small area.

58:59.100 --> 59:03.100
The Buddha wanted us to work with the small area because smaller the area,

59:03.100 --> 59:06.100
the subtler the mind is bound to become.

59:06.100 --> 59:09.100
More sensitive the mind is bound to become.

59:09.100 --> 59:12.100
Now small area, day after tomorrow you will have still smaller area.

59:12.100 --> 59:14.100
Now you work on the triangular area.

59:14.100 --> 59:18.100
Within this triangular area, the whole day you are working

59:18.100 --> 59:21.100
the touch of the breath, touch of the breath.

59:21.100 --> 59:25.100
Anywhere on the inner walls of the nostrils, touch of the breath.

59:25.100 --> 59:28.100
Anywhere on the outer rings of the nostrils, touch of the breath.

59:28.100 --> 59:32.100
Anywhere on the area below the nostrils, above the upper lip,

59:32.100 --> 59:35.100
touch of the breath, touch of the breath.

59:35.100 --> 59:41.100
Now tonight and tomorrow whole day, you will experience something subtler than that.

59:41.100 --> 59:44.100
As this touch was there all the time,

59:44.100 --> 59:47.100
but you never cared to be aware of it because you never practiced.

59:47.100 --> 59:52.100
Now by practicing, you made your mind sharper to feel this touch.

59:52.100 --> 59:56.100
Similarly, there are subtler things which are there all the time,

59:56.100 --> 59:58.100
but you never cared to be aware of it.

59:58.100 --> 01:00:03.100
Now this technique will help you and you will start feeling.

01:00:03.100 --> 01:00:08.100
One thing, one reality which will become very clear, very evident.

01:00:08.100 --> 01:00:14.100
You will notice that the breath that went in

01:00:14.100 --> 01:00:19.100
when it came out, it came out slightly warmer.

01:00:19.100 --> 01:00:24.100
The temperature of the incoming breath and the outgoing breath differs.

01:00:24.100 --> 01:00:27.100
The outgoing breath is slightly warmer.

01:00:27.100 --> 01:00:30.100
This is truth, but you never care to be aware of it.

01:00:30.100 --> 01:00:32.100
And it is just natural.

01:00:32.100 --> 01:00:37.100
The temperature of the outside atmosphere is lower than the temperature inside the body.

01:00:37.100 --> 01:00:42.100
So this breath from the outside atmosphere going in your body

01:00:42.100 --> 01:00:46.100
comes in contact with the warmer temperature there and comes out slightly warmer.

01:00:46.100 --> 01:00:53.100
You will notice that the outgoing breath is slightly warmer than the incoming breath.

01:00:53.100 --> 01:00:59.100
And then very soon you will start experiencing something more.

01:00:59.100 --> 01:01:04.100
Something, some reality which has nothing to do with the breath.

01:01:04.100 --> 01:01:08.100
You use the breath to move towards the subtler reality.

01:01:08.100 --> 01:01:11.100
Now even without using the breath, what is happening?

01:01:11.100 --> 01:01:15.100
You have been working on this small area, this triangular area.

01:01:15.100 --> 01:01:23.100
By tonight, by tomorrow you will start experiencing some biochemical reaction taking place here.

01:01:23.100 --> 01:01:27.100
Some electromagnetic reaction which is taking place throughout the body.

01:01:27.100 --> 01:01:33.100
Throughout the physical structure, every moment there is some biochemical reaction or the other.

01:01:33.100 --> 01:01:36.100
Some electromagnetic reaction or the other.

01:01:36.100 --> 01:01:40.100
And because of that some sensation or the other throughout the body.

01:01:40.100 --> 01:01:45.100
Wherever there is life there is bound to be a sensation.

01:01:45.100 --> 01:01:50.100
Now in this area you will start feeling some sensation.

01:01:50.100 --> 01:01:54.100
Not necessarily this particular sensation or that particular sensation.

01:01:54.100 --> 01:01:59.100
Any sensation. Any sensation that crops up.

01:01:59.100 --> 01:02:04.100
Maybe heat. You start feeling heat in this area.

01:02:04.100 --> 01:02:07.100
Within this area only.

01:02:07.100 --> 01:02:11.100
Heat. It can be body heat, it can be atmospheric heat.

01:02:11.100 --> 01:02:15.100
Heat. You just observe. There is heat at this moment.

01:02:15.100 --> 01:02:17.100
There is heat. That's all.

01:02:17.100 --> 01:02:20.100
May be cold. May be perspiration.

01:02:20.100 --> 01:02:22.100
Just observe. Do nothing.

01:02:22.100 --> 01:02:24.100
May be an itching sensation.

01:02:24.100 --> 01:02:27.100
Again just observe. An itching sensation.

01:02:27.100 --> 01:02:30.100
Don't react to it. An itching sensation.

01:02:30.100 --> 01:02:34.100
And you start reacting. You start rubbing it or scratching it.

01:02:34.100 --> 01:02:37.100
And it is not sammasati. Sammasati is just observe.

01:02:37.100 --> 01:02:41.100
Do nothing. Observe the reality which has manifested itself.

01:02:41.100 --> 01:02:44.100
And itching has started.

01:02:44.100 --> 01:02:46.100
Let me see how long it lasts.

01:02:46.100 --> 01:02:49.100
It becomes stronger, stronger, stronger but ultimately passes away.

01:02:49.100 --> 01:02:52.100
No itching is eternal.

01:02:52.100 --> 01:02:54.100
It is not going to stay forever.

01:02:54.100 --> 01:02:56.100
Let me see how long it lasts.

01:02:56.100 --> 01:02:58.100
Any sensation. Not going to last forever.

01:02:58.100 --> 01:03:01.100
It arises sooner or later passes away.

01:03:01.100 --> 01:03:03.100
It arises sooner or later passes away.

01:03:03.100 --> 01:03:07.100
And you are just a silent witness of things that are happening.

01:03:07.100 --> 01:03:09.100
May be itching.

01:03:09.100 --> 01:03:12.100
May be a ticklish sensation.

01:03:12.100 --> 01:03:15.100
At times may be a prickling sensation.

01:03:15.100 --> 01:03:18.100
At times may be a throbbing sensation.

01:03:18.100 --> 01:03:20.100
A pulsing sensation.

01:03:20.100 --> 01:03:23.100
May be a sensation of lightness.

01:03:23.100 --> 01:03:25.100
May be a sensation of heaviness.

01:03:25.100 --> 01:03:27.100
May be pressure.

01:03:27.100 --> 01:03:28.100
May be tension.

01:03:28.100 --> 01:03:29.100
May be strain.

01:03:29.100 --> 01:03:31.100
May be even pain.

01:03:31.100 --> 01:03:34.100
May be a sensation of expansion, contraction.

01:03:34.100 --> 01:03:36.100
Expansion, contraction.

01:03:36.100 --> 01:03:38.100
May be a sensation of numbness.

01:03:38.100 --> 01:03:40.100
May be a sensation of dryness.

01:03:40.100 --> 01:03:42.100
May be a sensation of moisture.

01:03:42.100 --> 01:03:44.100
Anything.

01:03:44.100 --> 01:03:47.100
You can't choose sensations.

01:03:47.100 --> 01:03:49.100
It is a choiceless observation.

01:03:49.100 --> 01:03:51.100
Let the nature play its own role.

01:03:51.100 --> 01:03:53.100
Let dhamma play its own role.

01:03:53.100 --> 01:03:56.100
From moment to moment whatever manifests itself.

01:03:56.100 --> 01:03:58.100
This is the reality of this moment.

01:03:58.100 --> 01:04:01.100
And your job is just to accept it and observe it.

01:04:01.100 --> 01:04:03.100
Observe it without reacting to it.

01:04:03.100 --> 01:04:06.100
Just observe, just observe, just observe.

01:04:06.100 --> 01:04:09.100
Don't look for something which is not there.

01:04:09.100 --> 01:04:11.100
Otherwise you will get lost.

01:04:11.100 --> 01:04:16.100
Whatever comes up there, you accept it and observe it.

01:04:16.100 --> 01:04:24.100
Quite possible that you may feel a sensation which you cannot name or label.

01:04:24.100 --> 01:04:27.100
Not necessary to name or label.

01:04:27.100 --> 01:04:32.100
Even the sensations that you can name or label should not be named or labeled.

01:04:32.100 --> 01:04:34.100
No. Something is happening.

01:04:34.100 --> 01:04:37.100
And you are just observing it objectively without reacting to it.

01:04:37.100 --> 01:04:39.100
Our purpose is served.

01:04:39.100 --> 01:04:41.100
This is what the technique wants it to do.

01:04:41.100 --> 01:04:47.100
Just accept the reality of this moment as it is without reacting to it.

01:04:47.100 --> 01:04:50.100
So any sensation.

01:04:50.100 --> 01:04:53.100
May be at times you don't feel any sensations.

01:04:53.100 --> 01:04:58.100
The sensation is there every moment on every little particle of the body.

01:04:58.100 --> 01:05:00.100
But your mind is very gross.

01:05:00.100 --> 01:05:02.100
So it can't feel subtle reality.

01:05:02.100 --> 01:05:05.100
So at times you don't feel anything within this limit.

01:05:05.100 --> 01:05:07.100
Then fall back to respiration.

01:05:07.100 --> 01:05:09.100
You have respiration alright.

01:05:09.100 --> 01:05:11.100
Keep on working with respiration, respiration.

01:05:11.100 --> 01:05:13.100
And suddenly a sensation crops up.

01:05:13.100 --> 01:05:16.100
Then start giving importance to the sensation that has cropped up.

01:05:16.100 --> 01:05:18.100
And remain with that sensation.

01:05:18.100 --> 01:05:21.100
The sensation passes away, some other sensation might crop up.

01:05:21.100 --> 01:05:23.100
That passes away, something else might crop up.

01:05:23.100 --> 01:05:24.100
Nothing crops up.

01:05:24.100 --> 01:05:25.100
Again respiration.

01:05:25.100 --> 01:05:27.100
Either respiration or sensation.

01:05:27.100 --> 01:05:31.100
But give more importance to sensation.

01:05:31.100 --> 01:05:37.100
Quite possible at times you may feel more than one sensation in this area.

01:05:37.100 --> 01:05:40.100
Two, three sensations at the same time.

01:05:40.100 --> 01:05:43.100
Don't get confused because of that.

01:05:43.100 --> 01:05:44.100
Choose one.

01:05:44.100 --> 01:05:48.100
And choose which is subtlest.

01:05:48.100 --> 01:05:50.100
One which is very strong.

01:05:50.100 --> 01:05:51.100
You can feel it so easily.

01:05:51.100 --> 01:05:52.100
Leave that.

01:05:52.100 --> 01:05:54.100
One which is very feeble.

01:05:54.100 --> 01:05:56.100
Give importance to the feeble one.

01:05:56.100 --> 01:05:58.100
And try to feel that feebler one.

01:05:58.100 --> 01:06:01.100
Your mind will become more and more sensitive.

01:06:01.100 --> 01:06:04.100
More and more subtle to feel that.

01:06:04.100 --> 01:06:08.100
Understand you have to keep your attention within this limited area.

01:06:08.100 --> 01:06:12.100
This will make your mind sharp and more sensitive.

01:06:12.100 --> 01:06:14.100
If you allow it to scatter throughout the body.

01:06:14.100 --> 01:06:16.100
Then again it will remain very gross.

01:06:16.100 --> 01:06:18.100
And it will feel only very gross sensations.

01:06:18.100 --> 01:06:22.100
And you can't go to the depth as Buddha wanted you to go to the depth.

01:06:22.100 --> 01:06:26.100
So while you are here, something might start on other parts of the body.

01:06:26.100 --> 01:06:28.100
You can't stop it.

01:06:28.100 --> 01:06:29.100
Never try to stop it.

01:06:29.100 --> 01:06:30.100
But ignore it.

01:06:30.100 --> 01:06:31.100
Don't give it any importance.

01:06:31.100 --> 01:06:33.100
Something is happening somewhere.

01:06:33.100 --> 01:06:36.100
My job is to explore the reality of this area.

01:06:36.100 --> 01:06:38.100
This triangular area.

01:06:38.100 --> 01:06:41.100
If anything happening on the inner walls of the nostrils.

01:06:41.100 --> 01:06:42.100
Any sensation crops up.

01:06:42.100 --> 01:06:44.100
I will observe.

01:06:44.100 --> 01:06:47.100
Any sensation crops up on the outer walls of the nostrils.

01:06:47.100 --> 01:06:48.100
Yes I will observe.

01:06:48.100 --> 01:06:52.100
Any sensation crops up on the outer rings of the nostrils.

01:06:52.100 --> 01:06:53.100
Yes I will observe.

01:06:53.100 --> 01:06:56.100
Any sensation crops up on the area below the nostrils.

01:06:56.100 --> 01:06:57.100
Above the upper lip.

01:06:57.100 --> 01:06:58.100
Yes I will observe it.

01:06:58.100 --> 01:07:00.100
But anything beyond that.

01:07:00.100 --> 01:07:01.100
I will ignore.

01:07:01.100 --> 01:07:04.100
Then you will find your mind is limited to a small area.

01:07:04.100 --> 01:07:08.100
And working on a small area it becomes sharper and sharper.

01:07:08.100 --> 01:07:09.100
Sharper and sharper.

01:07:09.100 --> 01:07:13.100
Work this night and then tomorrow whole day.

01:07:13.100 --> 01:07:15.100
This is sammasati.

01:07:15.100 --> 01:07:17.100
And the next is sammasamadhi.

01:07:17.100 --> 01:07:20.100
Now samadhi is concentration of the mind.

01:07:20.100 --> 01:07:25.100
But sammasamadhi is different.

01:07:25.100 --> 01:07:27.100
With the base, wholesome base.

01:07:27.100 --> 01:07:30.100
And what is wholesome base?

01:07:30.100 --> 01:07:33.100
Free from moha.

01:07:33.100 --> 01:07:35.100
The other day we talked moha.

01:07:35.100 --> 01:07:36.100
Ignorance.

01:07:36.100 --> 01:07:37.100
No illusion.

01:07:37.100 --> 01:07:39.100
No delusion.

01:07:39.100 --> 01:07:40.100
No hallucination.

01:07:40.100 --> 01:07:42.100
No confusion.

01:07:42.100 --> 01:07:45.100
And no imagination.

01:07:45.100 --> 01:07:51.100
The object of your concentration should be real.

01:07:51.100 --> 01:07:54.100
Whatever you are practicing as sammasati.

01:07:54.100 --> 01:07:57.100
Awareness of the reality of this moment.

01:07:57.100 --> 01:07:58.100
Reality of this moment.

01:07:58.100 --> 01:08:01.100
That you are experiencing within this limited area.

01:08:01.100 --> 01:08:04.100
Now this reality and your awareness of this reality.

01:08:04.100 --> 01:08:06.100
This moment.

01:08:06.100 --> 01:08:08.100
Next moment again you are aware of the reality.

01:08:08.100 --> 01:08:10.100
Next moment again you are aware of the reality.

01:08:10.100 --> 01:08:12.100
Like this from moment to moment.

01:08:12.100 --> 01:08:13.100
From moment to moment.

01:08:13.100 --> 01:08:14.100
From moment to moment.

01:08:14.100 --> 01:08:17.100
Without any disturbance.

01:08:17.100 --> 01:08:21.100
If you keep on observing the reality from moment to moment.

01:08:21.100 --> 01:08:22.100
This may change.

01:08:22.100 --> 01:08:24.100
This sensation or that sensation.

01:08:24.100 --> 01:08:26.100
But you are within this area.

01:08:26.100 --> 01:08:28.100
And the reality that is manifesting here.

01:08:28.100 --> 01:08:29.100
From moment to moment.

01:08:29.100 --> 01:08:30.100
From moment to moment.

01:08:30.100 --> 01:08:33.100
How long you continue to be aware without any interruption.

01:08:33.100 --> 01:08:36.100
That much is your samadhi stronger and stronger.

01:08:36.100 --> 01:08:38.100
And it is samma right.

01:08:38.100 --> 01:08:41.100
Because you are with the reality that you experience.

01:08:41.100 --> 01:08:43.100
No imagination is involved.

01:08:43.100 --> 01:08:47.100
A mind can get concentrated with an imaginary object.

01:08:47.100 --> 01:08:49.100
A shape or form.

01:08:49.100 --> 01:08:51.100
Of this god or that god.

01:08:51.100 --> 01:08:53.100
This goddess or that goddess.

01:08:53.100 --> 01:08:55.100
Founder of this religion or that religion.

01:08:55.100 --> 01:08:59.100
You can imagine the shape or form or this face of this person.

01:08:59.100 --> 01:09:01.100
Keep on repeating it.

01:09:01.100 --> 01:09:02.100
This imagination mentally.

01:09:02.100 --> 01:09:04.100
Mentally your mind gets concentrated.

01:09:04.100 --> 01:09:06.100
Or you keep on working with the word.

01:09:06.100 --> 01:09:07.100
Keep on repeating it.

01:09:07.100 --> 01:09:08.100
Verbalization.

01:09:08.100 --> 01:09:09.100
Verbalization.

01:09:09.100 --> 01:09:10.100
Mind gets concentrated.

01:09:10.100 --> 01:09:12.100
This is not the natural reality.

01:09:12.100 --> 01:09:15.100
You see the sheena that you practiced.

01:09:15.100 --> 01:09:18.100
Is to take you to the second step of samadhi.

01:09:18.100 --> 01:09:20.100
And the samadhi that you are practicing.

01:09:20.100 --> 01:09:23.100
Is to take you to the third step of panya.

01:09:23.100 --> 01:09:25.100
It is all progressive.

01:09:25.100 --> 01:09:28.100
Moving towards the final goal.

01:09:28.100 --> 01:09:31.100
So if you take any other object.

01:09:31.100 --> 01:09:33.100
Which is either imaginary.

01:09:33.100 --> 01:09:35.100
Or it is your own creation.

01:09:35.100 --> 01:09:37.100
You impose something.

01:09:37.100 --> 01:09:38.100
Which is not there.

01:09:38.100 --> 01:09:40.100
Then it will not take you to the final goal.

01:09:40.100 --> 01:09:44.100
So objects should be whatever comes up within this area.

01:09:44.100 --> 01:09:45.100
And you are aware.

01:09:45.100 --> 01:09:46.100
You are just aware.

01:09:46.100 --> 01:09:47.100
Movement to movement.

01:09:47.100 --> 01:09:48.100
Movement to movement.

01:09:48.100 --> 01:09:49.100
You are aware.

01:09:49.100 --> 01:09:50.100
You are aware.

01:09:50.100 --> 01:09:51.100
You are aware.

01:09:51.100 --> 01:09:52.100
How long you are aware?

01:09:52.100 --> 01:09:53.100
Continuously.

01:09:53.100 --> 01:09:55.100
Keeping the attention within this limited area.

01:09:55.100 --> 01:09:57.100
Is samma samadhi.

01:09:57.100 --> 01:10:00.100
Otherwise mind can get concentrated.

01:10:00.100 --> 01:10:02.100
Whether they said ignorance.

01:10:02.100 --> 01:10:04.100
These imaginary objects.

01:10:04.100 --> 01:10:07.100
Or with the base of greed.

01:10:07.100 --> 01:10:08.100
Raga.

01:10:08.100 --> 01:10:10.100
Or with the base of aversion.

01:10:10.100 --> 01:10:12.100
Dosha.

01:10:14.100 --> 01:10:17.100
You would have seen a hunter.

01:10:17.100 --> 01:10:20.100
Fully concentrated on his double barrel gun.

01:10:20.100 --> 01:10:22.100
A prey coming and he will shoot and kill.

01:10:22.100 --> 01:10:24.100
Concentration is there.

01:10:24.100 --> 01:10:27.100
But this is not samma samadhi.

01:10:27.100 --> 01:10:29.100
A cat.

01:10:29.100 --> 01:10:32.100
Standing near the mouse hole.

01:10:32.100 --> 01:10:34.100
Fully concentrated.

01:10:34.100 --> 01:10:36.100
The mouse comes out and jumps.

01:10:36.100 --> 01:10:37.100
And devours it.

01:10:37.100 --> 01:10:38.100
Fully concentrated.

01:10:38.100 --> 01:10:41.100
Not samma samadhi.

01:10:41.100 --> 01:10:46.100
Every unwholesome physical action or vocal action is done.

01:10:46.100 --> 01:10:49.100
With some amount of samadhi concentration.

01:10:49.100 --> 01:10:51.100
Even a pick pocket.

01:10:51.100 --> 01:10:53.100
Picks your pocket.

01:10:53.100 --> 01:10:54.100
Mind is concentrated.

01:10:54.100 --> 01:10:57.100
Very aware what he is doing or she is doing.

01:10:57.100 --> 01:11:00.100
This is not samma samadhi.

01:11:00.100 --> 01:11:02.100
It must be free from craving.

01:11:02.100 --> 01:11:03.100
Free from aversion.

01:11:03.100 --> 01:11:05.100
When you were observing your breath.

01:11:05.100 --> 01:11:06.100
You were free from moha.

01:11:06.100 --> 01:11:07.100
Ignorance.

01:11:07.100 --> 01:11:09.100
The truth that you are experiencing.

01:11:09.100 --> 01:11:11.100
There is no confusion about it.

01:11:11.100 --> 01:11:12.100
The breath is there.

01:11:12.100 --> 01:11:13.100
The touch of the breath.

01:11:13.100 --> 01:11:15.100
Yes the touch of the breath is there.

01:11:15.100 --> 01:11:16.100
And now these sensations.

01:11:16.100 --> 01:11:18.100
The sensations are there.

01:11:18.100 --> 01:11:19.100
And you are observing.

01:11:19.100 --> 01:11:22.100
And you are not observing with craving or with aversion.

01:11:22.100 --> 01:11:24.100
As with the breath there was no craving.

01:11:24.100 --> 01:11:25.100
No aversion.

01:11:25.100 --> 01:11:27.100
Similarly with the touch there was no craving.

01:11:27.100 --> 01:11:28.100
No aversion.

01:11:28.100 --> 01:11:31.100
Similarly now the sensations that you experience here.

01:11:31.100 --> 01:11:32.100
No craving.

01:11:32.100 --> 01:11:33.100
No aversion.

01:11:33.100 --> 01:11:34.100
Things are just happening.

01:11:34.100 --> 01:11:36.100
And you are observing objectively.

01:11:36.100 --> 01:11:37.100
Objectively.

01:11:37.100 --> 01:11:40.100
This makes the samadhi samma samadhi.

01:11:40.100 --> 01:11:43.100
And this helps you to move in the next field.

01:11:43.100 --> 01:11:46.100
The third field of panya.

01:11:46.100 --> 01:11:47.100
That is wisdom.

01:11:47.100 --> 01:11:49.100
That is insight.

01:11:49.100 --> 01:11:50.100
Which will purify the mind.

01:11:50.100 --> 01:11:54.100
Not merely at the surface level.

01:11:54.100 --> 01:11:58.100
Sheila takes you to samadhi where you develop mastery over the mind.

01:11:58.100 --> 01:12:02.100
But this mastery over the mind is at the surface level.

01:12:02.100 --> 01:12:03.100
Slightly deeper.

01:12:03.100 --> 01:12:06.100
And panya takes you to the depth of the mind.

01:12:06.100 --> 01:12:09.100
And at the deepest level the third part of dhamma.

01:12:09.100 --> 01:12:12.100
Is to purify the mind at the deepest level.

01:12:12.100 --> 01:12:14.100
The so called unconscious level.

01:12:14.100 --> 01:12:16.100
The source of your misery.

01:12:16.100 --> 01:12:18.100
From where all these impurities arise.

01:12:18.100 --> 01:12:20.100
Originate and they multiply.

01:12:20.100 --> 01:12:23.100
The stock of your past impurities that you accumulated.

01:12:23.100 --> 01:12:26.100
All of them have to come up on the surface and pass.

01:12:26.100 --> 01:12:28.100
Come up on the surface and pass.

01:12:28.100 --> 01:12:29.100
That will be panya.

01:12:29.100 --> 01:12:31.100
We won't discuss about it today.

01:12:31.100 --> 01:12:32.100
We will discuss tomorrow.

01:12:32.100 --> 01:12:35.100
Because day after tomorrow you are entering the field of panya.

01:12:35.100 --> 01:12:37.100
Theory and practice should go together.

01:12:37.100 --> 01:12:39.100
So tomorrow we discuss about panya.

01:12:39.100 --> 01:12:41.100
So that you practice day after tomorrow.

01:12:41.100 --> 01:12:43.100
Now you are in the field of Sheila.

01:12:43.100 --> 01:12:46.100
You are observing all the precepts that you have taken very meticulously.

01:12:46.100 --> 01:12:47.100
Very scrupulously.

01:12:47.100 --> 01:12:49.100
And you are practicing your samadhi.

01:12:49.100 --> 01:12:51.100
Awareness of the reality within this limited area.

01:12:51.100 --> 01:12:53.100
From moment to moment.

01:12:53.100 --> 01:12:55.100
From moment to moment.

01:12:55.100 --> 01:12:57.100
Make use of the time.

01:12:57.100 --> 01:13:00.100
Make use of the opportunity with a good base of Sheila.

